            <ArticleTitle>High density lipoproteins in ischaemic heart disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1063-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>High density lipoprotein cholesterol concentrations were significantly lower in ischaemic heart disease patients than in healthy subjects when age and sex-matched. This difference was, however, not observed in the older age group (greater than 60 years).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
